      "text": "Let's analyze the problem step-by-step:\n\n1. Ray climbs the stairs in two different ways:\n    - When he climbs the stairs 4 steps at a time, the total number of steps \\( n \\) leaves a remainder of 3 when divided by 4. In other words, \\( n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4} \\).\n    - When he climbs the stairs 5 steps at a time, the total number of steps \\( n \\) leaves a remainder of 2 when divided by 5. In other words, \\( n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\).\n\n2. We need to find the smallest \\( n > 10 \\) that satisfies both congruences. We will use the Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT) to solve this system of congruences.\n\nThe congruences are:\n\\[ n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4} \\]\n\\[ n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\nFirst, we express \\( n \\) in terms of the first congruence:\n\\[ n = 4k + 3 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\).\n\nNext, we substitute \\( n \\) into the second congruence:\n\\[ 4k + 3 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 4k + 3 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\\[ 4k \\equiv -1 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\\[ 4k \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSince 4 and 5 are coprime, we can divide both sides by 4:\n\\[ k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSo, \\( k = 5m + 1 \\) for some integer \\( m \\). Substituting back into the expression for \\( n \\):\n\\[ n = 4(5m + 1) + 3 \\]\n\\[ n = 20m + 7 \\]\nThis shows that \\( n \\) can be written in the form \\( n = 20m + 7 \\), where \\( m \\) is an integer. The smallest value of \\( n \\) greater than 10 is obtained when \\( m = 1 \\):\n\\[ n = 20(1) + 7 = 27 \\]\nSo, the smallest possible value of \\( n \\) that satisfies both conditions is \\( 27 \\). We can verify this by checking the conditions:\n- \\( 27 \\div 4 = 6 \\) remainder 3, so \\( 27 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4} \\)\n- \\( 27 \\div 5 = 5 \\) remainder 2, so \\( 27 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\)\n\nThus, the smallest possible value of \\( n \\) is \\( \\boxed{27} \\).\n\nHere is the Python code to confirm the solution:\n```python\n# Define the function to find the smallest n > 10 that satisfies the given conditions\ndef find_smallest_n():\n    m = 1\n    while True:\n        n = 20 * m + 7\n        if n > 10:\n            return n\n        m += 1\n\n# Find and print the smallest n that satisfies the conditions\nsmallest_n = find_smallest_n()\nprint(smallest_n)\n```",
