      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let $n$ be the number of steps in the flight of stairs.\n\nWhen Ray climbs up the stairs $4$ at a time, there are $3$ steps left at the top. This means that $n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}$. \n\nWhen Ray climbs up the stairs $5$ at a time, there are $2$ steps left at the top. This means that $n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5}$.\n\nWe can combine these two congruences to form a single congruence by multiplying both sides of the first congruence by $-1$ and adding the two congruences together:$$n \\equiv -11 \\pmod{20}.$$Since $10$ is a multiple of $2$, we also know that $n$ is greater than $10$. The smallest possible value of $n$ greater than $10$ that satisfies this congruence is $\\boxed{122}$.\nThe answer is: 122",
